-- title:
--   Unipotent naturality at the Igusa chart of ∞
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a nonzero level $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a non-unit. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M'` (rational affine geometric places whose $j$-value lies in the supersingular set), assume `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of the base-changed full-level field along $A$ whose residue map is computed by coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$. Let $\zeta$ index a primitive $q$-th root of unity, let $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ be valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by the projective line over $\mathbb Z/q$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ ones indexed by $W$, subject to: the description of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ as the ratios of Laurent series over $A$ with denominator of nonzero reduction, transitivity of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-action on the family via `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, its permutation behaviour under all level automorphisms, and the supersingular clauses (constancy on $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, compatibility with $R_0$ and the places of $W$, $\Gamma_0(M')$-invariance, existence of a transversal parameter); these are summarised here. Further let $C_\infty$ be a component chart for $A$ over `fieldBar q M'` with residues in `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, $R_I$ a regular prolongation with `RI.integers = OIg (lineInfty q)`, with $C_\infty$ having the same integers and the same residue map as $R_I$, $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}=C_\infty.\mathrm{nodes}$, and $(\mathrm{discI},\mathrm{coordI})$ a disc family for $R_I$ away from $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, together with stalk data $S_I$, $\chi_{0I}$ and clauses identifying the stalks and the discs, identifying $C_\infty.\mathrm{dom}$ as the union of the discs over $Q\notin N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, prescribing $C_\infty.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on and off that domain, and asserting that the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms stabilises $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ and permutes the discs compatibly. Finally let $g\,\ell$ be automorphisms in that subgroup, of the form `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ carrying $\infty$ to $\ell$, and $C_{\mathrm{Ig}}\,\ell=C_\infty$ pulled back along $g\,\ell$. Assume that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ whose reduction `redQ q γ` is unipotent, the semilinear automorphism attached to `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ⁻¹` preserves the integers of $C_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ and acts on its residues as the identity. The conclusion is that for every such $\zeta'$ and $\gamma$ three things hold: a place $P$ lies in the domain of $C_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ if and only if its translate under that semilinear automorphism does; the same chart-inducing clause as assumed; and the place map of $C_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ takes the same value at $P$ and at its translate, for every $P$ in the domain.
--
--   This is a bookkeeping step in the assembly of the semistable covering of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ over a valuation subring above $q$: it upgrades the ring-and-residue statement for a unipotent level automorphism at the Igusa chart of $\infty$ to stability of the chart's domain and invariance of its place map. It is used in the existence theorem producing the semistable covering together with its naturality clauses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_naturality_unipotent_igusaInfty_of_discFamily.lean

